      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. This order is twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg in one dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth three or four times daily**, which is 1,600\u20133,200 mg/day. For example, 800 mg three times daily is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
